  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1202 PM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nDry conditions and slightly above normal temperatures continue.\nThe 12z sounding out of LZK depicts a stout dry level between 850-\n500mb. The drier air aloft will continue to mix down to the\nsurface and lower dewpoints and relative humidity (RH) values\nthrough the afternoon. Due to the expected drop of RH values with\n10 hour fuel moisture forecasts around 10%, a Fire Danger\nStatement is in effect from noon until 7 PM.\n\nWhile we remain under surface high pressure and northwest flow\naloft, expect stagnant conditions to persist for much of the\nforecast period. An omega blocking pattern will keep the synoptic\npattern on hold through early next week. We will be monitoring\nthe trough on the west side of the block and its evolution for\nnext week. The LREF and its ensemble members are not too keen on\nimpacts across the Mid-South with a gradual breakdown of the\nridge and the energy heading towards the upper Midwest. Some of\nthe longer range deterministic models are following closely\nbehind the ensembles. In the meantime, expect dry conditions,\nslightly above normal temperatures, and elevated fire danger to\npersist.\n\nDNM",
